# expiry3 — KEEPTTL and PERSIST
#
# Learn: SET key value KEEPTTL changes the value but keeps the remaining
# time to live. PERSIST key removes a TTL and makes the key permanent.
# (EXPIRE key 0 does not mean "never": it deletes the key right away.)
#
# Task: the check creates user:1:token and user:1:profile, both with a
# TTL. Rotate the token's value to "tok-new" without extending or losing
# its expiry, and make the profile permanent.
#

SET user:1:token tok-new
EXPIRE user:1:profile 0
